.TH ERF 3  "May 12, 1986"
.UC 6
.SH NAME
erf, erfc \- error functions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.ft B
#include <math.h>

double
erf(\fIdouble x\fP)

double
erfc(\fIdouble x\fP)
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBerf\fI\|(x) returns the error function of x; where
.if n \{\
.PP
\fBerf\fP(x) = 2/sqrt(pi)\(**\|integral from 0 to x of exp(\-t\(**t) dt. \}
.if t \{\
\fBerf\fP\|(x) := 
(2/\(sr\(*p)\|\(is\d\s8\z0\s10\u\u\s8x\s10\d\|exp(\-t\u\s82\s10\d)\|dt. \}
.PP
\fBerfc\fP\|(x) returns 1.0\-erf\|(x).
.PP
The entry for \fBerfc\fP is provided because of the extreme loss
of relative accuracy if \fBerf\fP\|(x) is called for large x
and the result subtracted from 1.
(e.g. for x = 10, 12 places are lost).
.SH SEE ALSO
math(3)
